counterfactuals.output:
A refrigeration system comprising:

a refrigeration circuit configured to circulate a refrigerant, the refrigeration circuit including a compressor, a condenser or gas cooler, an expansion device, and an evaporator arranged to transfer heat from a cooling fluid to the refrigerant;

a cooling-fluid circuit configured to circulate the cooling fluid through a load heat exchanger and through the evaporator of the refrigeration circuit;

a free-cooling system configured to circulate a free-cooling fluid through a free-cooling heat exchanger, the free-cooling heat exchanger being arranged to transfer heat from the cooling fluid to the free-cooling fluid when an ambient or external cooling source is available;

one or more valves disposed in at least one of the refrigeration circuit, the cooling-fluid circuit, and the free-cooling system, the one or more valves being selectively controllable to establish a plurality of operating modes;

wherein, in a mechanical refrigeration mode, the cooling fluid rejects heat to the refrigerant in the evaporator and the refrigerant rejects heat through the condenser or gas cooler;

wherein, in a free-cooling mode, the cooling fluid rejects heat to the free-cooling fluid in the free-cooling heat exchanger while operation of the compressor is reduced or disabled;

wherein, in a combined cooling mode, heat is transferred from the cooling fluid both to the refrigerant in the evaporator and to the free-cooling fluid in the free-cooling heat exchanger;

and wherein the one or more valves are actuated to selectively direct flow of the refrigerant, the cooling fluid, and/or the free-cooling fluid so as to switch between the mechanical refrigeration mode, the free-cooling mode, and the combined cooling mode in response to at least one operating condition including cooling demand, cooling-fluid temperature, free-cooling-fluid temperature, ambient temperature, or refrigerant pressure.
